                                "sense_id": "f0654dc1-ca99-3809-8e57-fbcdd28afb7f",
                                "text": "Było nas do pięćdziesiąt człeka, chłop w chłopa, wszystko strzelcy zawołani, tylko ja fryc jeden"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1a8a384-9654-3ffd-a812-6afc42cdea35",
                        "entry_id": "f563180a-8b40-3e13-b7fe-8e5fa44aeb33",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Niemiec"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "offensive",
                            "pejorative",
                            "scornfully"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18419a0b-cff0-482b-8424-d836768c0e93",
                                "sense_id": "c1a8a384-9654-3ffd-a812-6afc42cdea35",
                                "text": "Pamiętasz tego typa, co mi w Berlinie pracę proponował? Oszukał mnie, fryc jeden."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58bcc74a-4023-3b83-bf7b-8a9f0b4a325b",
                        "entry_id": "f563180a-8b40-3e13-b7fe-8e5fa44aeb33",
                        "glosses": [
                            "fryzjer"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "54648b38-7d13-4620-a694-da6f0e741e90",
                                "sense_id": "58bcc74a-4023-3b83-bf7b-8a9f0b4a325b",
                                "text": "Włosy mi urosły, muszę iść do fryca."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.3\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "798f3495-6cbb-491f-97fa-75fd1661570c",
                        "source_entry_id": "f563180a-8b40-3e13-b7fe-8e5fa44aeb33",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1a8a384-9654-3ffd-a812-6afc42cdea35",
                        "target_lang_word": "Fritz",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Fritz",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31ae37c4-694e-3744-b988-1b0a6bf4ff2b",
                                        "entry_id": "682ed024-0b28-3fa7-a7c5-20d7849bbfb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A German person, usually male."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "ethnic",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1932bb5e-85f7-4597-b8cc-79fa9a62f664",
                                                "sense_id": "31ae37c4-694e-3744-b988-1b0a6bf4ff2b",
                                                "text": "Someone sent up a shout and word came that oil had begun to show on the water—that meant one less submarine afloat! Again the roar of guns—again the shout! Two Fritzes sunk. . . !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Fritz",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc83fba9-6e4a-3fee-b1ab-6c29e8f0917c",
                                        "entry_id": "93bd06f6-6899-3a4d-b6fc-a55d31e07b96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A name used to represent the German people (particularly the German armed forces) as a group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "offensive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5325f6b3-639d-482a-ba9d-71f643d23277",
                                                "sense_id": "fc83fba9-6e4a-3fee-b1ab-6c29e8f0917c",
                                                "text": "But if Fritz is stationed in that patch of woodland, we've got no chance!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d91797b-d665-4e40-9814-a24a8dcb80ce",
                                                "sense_id": "fc83fba9-6e4a-3fee-b1ab-6c29e8f0917c",
                                                "text": "You! Fritz! Tell us where the ammunition's kept!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6001fb31-feca-411f-af08-2f9147c98387",
                                                "sense_id": "fc83fba9-6e4a-3fee-b1ab-6c29e8f0917c",
                                                "text": "[…]so Fritz could sleep easily in his trench, so far as mines were concerned; and Fritz, confident in his Herr Professors, altogether neglected any attempt to counter-mine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4b679b9-cf87-4942-8389-4e45a234abb0",
                                                "sense_id": "fc83fba9-6e4a-3fee-b1ab-6c29e8f0917c",
                                                "text": "'Fritz is pounding away at the crossing,' he said. 'We'd do better to wait till things quieten down.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4f0ab7b-e611-3583-9afd-8ffd16afe152",
                                        "entry_id": "93bd06f6-6899-3a4d-b6fc-a55d31e07b96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A diminutive of the male given name Friedrich."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b11a2f8-9265-4134-9cad-3a2f453c5fae",
                                                "sense_id": "b4f0ab7b-e611-3583-9afd-8ffd16afe152",
                                                "text": "Uncle Fritz “talked eyes” when he was the most deeply aggrieved; and little Fritz found it most unpleasant to have an American relative addicted to the same bad habit. She came into the room just then and there, and, seeing the two Fritzes in such confidential discussion, would have speedily withdrawn, had not the gentleman risen and begged her to remain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bb16b78-622d-4cc5-8849-a71c4d956c50",
                                                "sense_id": "b4f0ab7b-e611-3583-9afd-8ffd16afe152",
                                                "text": "“Has she any children?” asked the practical Johannes. / “Just one—a nice boy, too. Thirteen. Fritz is his name.” Jakob chuckled. “Just the same as your brother. That’s a good one—there’ll be two Fritzes in one family!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db063068-3502-33df-abd2-017aabf34740",
                                        "entry_id": "93bd06f6-6899-3a4d-b6fc-a55d31e07b96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname from German."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfb099f7-c483-4f18-9c91-fa9b7a932e9e",
                                                "sense_id": "db063068-3502-33df-abd2-017aabf34740",
                                                "text": "The highly anticipated all-American matchup between Taylor Fritz and Frances Tiafoe — marking the first US Open semifinals between two US men in nearly 20 years — will cost you quite a few Honey Deuces to attend."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
